# Stratum — suggested .gitignore entries for an analysis project.
#
# Written by `stratum init`. Everything below is appended to your existing
# .gitignore; nothing here is required for Stratum to work.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Volatile cache. Never commit this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .stratum/ holds cached result blobs, rendered graphs, dataset state snapshots,
# the ado index, AI transcripts and execution timestamps. It is machine-local,
# large, non-deterministic and fully regenerable — deleting it costs you nothing
# but the time to re-run. Stratum also writes .stratum/.gitignore containing `*`
# when it first creates the directory, so this line is belt and braces.
.stratum/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sidecars. Read this before uncommenting.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `<file>.do.workspace` is the DURABLE half of the sidecar: section names and
# order, cell markers, narrative region boundaries, collapse intent, pinned model
# comparisons, and the per-file inline-results mode. It contains no timestamps,
# no durations, no execution ids and no output, so it does not churn when you run
# your code. It is small (typically under 4 KB), JSON with sorted keys and LF
# endings, and it diffs cleanly.
#
# We recommend COMMITTING it. Section names are part of the document — a
# collaborator who clones without the sidecar gets your analysis but loses its
# structure. Nothing about execution output ever enters version control either
# way, and deleting the sidecar loses only layout, never analysis.
#
# Uncomment the next line only if you would rather keep the repository to .do
# files alone.
# *.do.workspace

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stata and analysis by-products
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.smcl
*.stswp
*.log.bak

# Uncomment if your logs are reproducible output rather than a record you keep.
# *.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment whichever of these describes data you must not publish. Raw data
# under an access agreement does not belong in git even when it is small.
# data/raw/
# *.dta
# *.csv
